From b1f8c19ac9145f6912172f2393e715ebfeaedf02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/59] CUDA/HIP: fold the q/k Hadamard rotation of a rotated
 KV cache into RMS_NORM+MUL+ROPE

RMS_NORM, MUL, ROPE, RESHAPE and the Hadamard MUL_MAT (llama_mul_mat_hadamard) run as one
rms_norm_mul_rope_f32 launch: the roped row goes to shared memory and the first warp writes its
FWHT with fwht_cuda's code (moved to fwht_row_warp in fwht.cuh), so results are bitwise identical.
The fusion memory check accepts a source that exactly aliases the output when the kernel reads each
row completely before writing it (the allocator reuses the K projection buffer in every other layer).
New RMS_NORM_MUL_ROPE hadamard=1 tests (norm/neox/imrope, n = 64..512).

Qwen3.8-27B MTP n=4 verify (rocprofv3): 1004 -> 972 kernels, gap sum 3.34 -> 3.23 ms,
verify wall 31.17 -> 31.01 ms. Greedy plain/MTP outputs identical.
